  "description": "How do rockets fly? Find out with Gizmo the robot: a rocket engine turns its fuel into hot gas and pushes it out the back, and the gas pushes the rocket the other way. A rocket carries its own oxygen, so it works in space, and big rockets drop empty stages to get lighter.\nA science explainer for kids ages 4-8, with questions to answer, things to copy, quick checks and a quiz at the end.\n\nWhere the facts come from (read Nov 19, 2026): NASA, What Is a Rocket? (Grades K-4 and Grades 5-8); NASA Glenn Research Center, Practical Rocketry.\n\nGizmo Explains makes gentle, colorful videos for little learners. New videos every day! Made with care for ages 4-8. Every fact is checked against trusted sources and every script is reviewed for kid safety before publishing.",
